SUMMARY:Two Routes to Silicon Sampling
DTSTART:20260923T150000Z
DTEND:20260923T160000Z
DTSTAMP:20260915T092934Z
UID:ae50d44021739e27d1ec20b6@systemsmap.antlerboy.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Complexity
DESCRIPTION:Complexity Science Hub\nLarge language models are increasingly
  used as substitutes for human participants. I distinguish two routes to s
 uch silicon samples: foundation models fine-tuned on behavioral data\, and
  off-the-shelf models steered by persona prompts. On the first route\, I d
 iscuss Centaur\, a language model fine-tuned on human choices from many be
 havioral experiments\, which predicts decisions better than establishe\nLa
